CODEGEN.md §2.1, §5.3, DECISIONS 413: values never selects table ids, so a ts-only package whose two tables of one record are both left out by values: still declares TierId twice, E8005 at the later table, as Go and C++ do.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tier.
record Tier {
  /// Its rank.
  rank: Int
}

/// The first tiers.
let first: table Tier = {
  one { rank: 1 }
}

/// The second tiers.
let second: table Tier = {
  two { rank: 2 }
}

/// The only selected value.
let kept: Tier = { rank: 3 }

emit ts { out: "@features/a/a.ts", mode: baked, values: [kept] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:15:5
  ts: TierId is generated for both a.first and a.second; hold one of them in a keyed list

